abstract: >-
  We demonstrate that the Hubble tension (H₀ discrepancy between early and
  late universe measurements) and the radial acceleration relation (RAR) in
  galaxies arise from the same physical mechanism: an entropy-driven
  modification of effective gravity. Using the Energy-Flow Cosmology (EFC)
  Core Lock framework with sigmoid entropy mapping S(z), we derive the
  gravitational coupling coefficient a_G ≈ 0.094 from Hubble tension data.
  Independently, MOND phenomenology at the transition regime (g_bar/a₀ ≈ 5)
  implies a_G ≈ 0.107. The 14% agreement, combined with the Friedmann-derived
  constraint a_H₀ = ½a_G, enables prediction of H₀ ≈ 74 km/s/Mpc from galaxy
  rotation data alone—matching the observed value of 73.0 km/s/Mpc within 1.2%.
